          "worked": "The square root is the denominator, so $4x^2-4>0$. Find the boundary values:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4x^2-4&=0\\\\4(x-1)(x+1)&=0\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }x=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nSketch $y=4x^2-4$. The upward parabola is above the $x$-axis when $x<-1$ or $x>1$. The roots are excluded because the denominator would be zero.\n\nThe domain is $(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(1,\\infty)$.",
